  "generated_text": "1. **Determine the dimensions of the pyramid:**\n   - The height of the pyramid is 12 inches.\n   - The base of the pyramid is a square with each side measuring 10 inches.\n\n2. **Find the smallest cube-shaped box that can contain the pyramid:**\n   - The pyramid needs to be placed in a cube-shaped box such that it fits right side up.\n   - The height of the cube must be at least 12 inches to accommodate the height of the pyramid.\n   - The base of the cube must be at least 10 inches on each side to accommodate the base of the pyramid.\n\n3. **Calculate the volume of the cube:**\n   - The volume \\( V \\) of a cube is given by the formula \\( V = s^3 \\), where \\( s \\) is the side length of the cube.\n   - Here, the side length \\( s \\) is 12 inches.\n   - Therefore, the volume \\( V \\) is \\( V = 12^3 = 1728 \\) cubic inches.\n\n4. **Conclusion:**\n   - The volume of the smallest cube-shaped box is \\(\\boxed{1728}\\) cubic inches.",
